{"title":"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/7/a270aa576b38a9d588921299f30b09bfff4855fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{0.34,0.304,0.034,0.43\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"192\" height=\"20\" />. The sum of the smallest and largest numbers in the set is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/2/f52ea0c8a636e8b06b5471fd5a2e8e9e5c1c0650.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 0.77 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 0.734 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 0.077 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 0.464 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 0.338$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"504\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The smallest number in the set is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/b/d6bf33727a70a4b6accb7e6871225fcdf8292619.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.034$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> and the largest number in the set is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/6/d362a11ff181cdc070ed418040a75000707ca575.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.43 = 0.430$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"100\" height=\"14\" />, as can be seen through the different tenths place of the numbers in the set and the fact that all numbers in the set are between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (exclusive). The sum of these numbers is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/6/5d647cc8a33b22a3b47c6067e35f4b61739cdbf4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.430 + 0.034 = \\boxed{\\textbf {(D) } 0.464}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"220\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 12\">